  "text": "Iqa‘ Muhajjar 14/4 Iqa‘ Index Pronunciation of Muhajjar Iqa‘ Muhajjar is a very popular iqa‘ in the Muwashah repertoire. It is immediately recognizable by the 3 consecutive dum -s that open the measure. The word \"muhajjar\" in Arabic means made of/turned into stone. Muwashah Badat Min al-Khidri Ensemble Al-Kindi Muwashah Hajarni Habibi Al-Turath Ensemble Muwashah Hal ‘Ala al-Astar Ensemble Morkos Muwashah Munyati ‘Azza Istibari Choir of the faculty of Music - Kaslik University (Lebanon) Conductor: Aïda Shalhoub Ziadé Music by Sayyed Darwish Orientalia: Muwashah and Song series Muwashah Ya Tura Ba‘da al-Bi‘adi Ensemble Al-Kindi Iqa‘ Muhajjar 14/4 Tabla demonstration by Faisal Zedan",
